#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Write a python script that will take any chapter of any book that exists in both eng/ and heb/ and turn it into a combined latex file of the type that we have in [12345]-*/.tex

Then add support for recursively merging all the chapters in a given book.

Then add support for recursively merging all the books that don't yet have latex files.

Don't overwrite the tex files we have in [12345]-*/*.tex

Just generate python code that can reliably merge the files in heb/ and eng/ into files in the latter books starting at 6-joshua and continuing until we're done with everything we have available at present.

End by making sure the \\includes at the end of master.tex are in the right order and not missing any books or chapters, that they're formatted consistently, and then uncomment all of them.

Don't commit or try to build the full uncommented book yet.

Once you've uncommented them all, you're done.

We'll resume in the morning.

Or rather, the afternoon.

It's late.
EOF
